+ * of those paths now writes one "[exit-trace]" line, straight to the stderr
+ * handle with WriteFile (not through the CRT buffer, so a fault inside printf
+ * or a kill a moment later cannot lose it): wall clock, ms since init, thread
+ * id and name, what happened. Covered: exit()/atexit (with the host return
+ * addresses as image RVAs), ExitProcess/_exit/abort's _exit (a TLS callback
+ * sees DLL_PROCESS_DETACH), SIGABRT (std::terminate's default ends there),
+ * the unhandled-exception filter, a last vectored handler (faults no runtime
+ * handler resolved), and the call sites that use ps3_exit_trace() (guest
